# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# /music is the shareable name for the record — the link that gets sent
# to someone so they can hear it. The file is music.html, and Pages
# serves it at /music on its own: it strips .html and 308s the extension
# form to the clean path. So the canonical URL needs no rule here at all.
#
# That 308 is also why the first attempt failed. /music was a 200
# rewrite onto /mixtape.html, and Pages' extension-stripping runs BEFORE
# _redirects — so the rewrite resolved to the file, then Pages bounced
# the browser to /mixtape and the address bar showed the old name. The
# fix was to let the platform own the clean URL instead of fighting it.
#
# What is left are the other names. Every /mixtape link already shared
# has to keep working, and every name should land on the canonical URL
# rather than quietly serving a second copy of the same page — one
# record, one address, however you arrived at it.
/mixtape        /music    301
/mixtape.html   /music    301
/mixedtape      /music    301
/mixedtape.html /music    301
